1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:03,280
Léa: Mathieu, quick question.

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,600
When you say "I'm going to bed",

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,760
do you really go to bed?

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,180
Mathieu: Of course.

5
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,640
Well, I begin the journey.

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,160
Léa: The journey?

7
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,360
Your bedroom is at the end of the hallway?

8
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,970
Mathieu: Yes, but between the sofa and the bedroom,

9
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:21,440
there's the kitchen.

10
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:24,720
And in the kitchen, there's cheese.

11
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,730
You have to plan the stages.

12
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,900
Léa: Good evening everyone

13
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,210
and welcome to The Cozy French.

14
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,480
I'm Léa.

15
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,170
Mathieu: And I'm Mathieu.

16
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:38,440
Today, we're speaking French and above all,

17
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,560
we're talking about our evenings,

18
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:44,100
real evenings, with the washing-up,

19
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,270
pyjamas and sometimes

20
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:50,210
a little detour via the fridge.

21
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,260
Léa: You're going to learn to describe your evening routine,

22
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:56,500
to talk about what relaxes you and to

23
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,800
say that you're tired.

24
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,000
Make yourselves comfortable.

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,060
You can simply listen

26
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:05,560
or repeat a few sentences with us.

27
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:08,880
Mathieu: And keep this question in mind:

28
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:11,040
What's the first thing you do

29
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,090
when you get home?

30
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:16,280
Léa: Me, I take off my shoes.

31
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:17,900
Mathieu: There's a simple answer,

32
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,800
and already very useful in French.

33
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,460
Léa: Last night, I came home wanting just one thing:

34
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:27,400
to put on comfortable clothes.

35
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,880
I'd worn jeans that were too tight all day.

36
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:34,290
Mathieu: The kind of jeans that make you choose

37
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:37,170
between sitting down and breathing?

38
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:38,240
Léa: Exactly.

39
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,950
So I put down my bag,

40
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,870
took off my shoes

41
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:44,290
and put on some really soft trousers.

42
00:01:44,290 --> 00:01:47,880
That's when I felt my evening was starting.

43
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,830
Mathieu: I love that moment too.

44
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:52,830
At home, I put on my slippers.

45
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:54,960
They're not very pretty,

46
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:58,000
but we're in a serious relationship.

47
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,920
Léa: Have you had them for long?

48
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,720
Mathieu: Long enough for them

49
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,650
to know all my secrets.

50
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,320
Léa: To describe your first actions,

51
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,500
you can say, "When I get home,

52
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,960
I put down my bag and I get changed."

53
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,800
"Se changer" here means putting on other clothes.

54
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,600
Mathieu: I get changed.

55
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:18,200
You get changed.

56
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:23,200
And Léa gets changed before she even checks her messages.

57
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,360
Léa: Often, yes.

58
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:28,210
And you, do you manage to leave work at the door?

59
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,540
Mathieu: Not always.

60
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:33,590
Sometimes I'm at home, but in my head,

61
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:35,920
I'm still in a meeting.

62
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,360
Léa: Oh yes, body on the sofa,

63
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:41,280
mind in front of an Excel spreadsheet.

64
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,440
Mathieu: That's it.

65
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:45,790
So some evenings, I walk a little around my

66
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:48,120
neighbourhood before going home.

67
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:51,640
Ten minutes with no particular goal.

68
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,530
It helps me unwind.

69
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:58,160
Léa: "Décompresser" means letting your focus go

70
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:01,360
after a tiring or stressful moment.

71
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,680
For example, after work,

72
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:06,720
I listen to music to unwind.

73
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,880
Mathieu: What about you?

74
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:10,760
Complete this sentence out loud.

75
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:13,300
When I get home,

76
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:13,920
I…

77
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,080
Léa: Very good.

78
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,360
Even a short sentence is enough to start.

79
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:22,510
Mathieu: Next, at my place, comes the big question:

80
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:24,330
What are we eating?

81
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,320
Léa: Do you decide at the last minute?

82
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,680
Mathieu: Often.

83
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:31,670
I open the fridge full of hope.

84
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,400
I close it again.

85
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:36,960
Then I open it again, in case an idea

86
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,560
has turned up in the meantime.

87
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,000
Léa: And does it?

88
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,160
Mathieu: Rarely.

89
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:45,960
But the carrots stay very patient.

90
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:48,840
Léa: Me, I like cooking when I have time.

91
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,260
When I'm tired,

92
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,330
I make something simple.

93
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,280
An omelette, a soup or the leftovers from the day before.

94
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:58,820
Mathieu: "Les restes" are the food

95
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,200
left over after a meal.

96
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:04,800
Tonight, I'm heating up the leftovers.

97
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,830
It's a sentence I use

98
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:09,200
with a lot of enthusiasm.

99
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,000
Léa: Because you like avoiding waste?

100
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:12,630
Mathieu: Yes.

101
00:04:12,630 --> 00:04:16,280
And because dinner is almost ready.

102
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:19,000
Both can be true.

103
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,090
Léa: Do you eat in front of a screen?

104
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,280
Mathieu: Sometimes.

105
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,520
But I also like calling a friend

106
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,000
while I cook.

107
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,820
Then eating in peace.

108
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,000
And you?

109
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,140
Léa: I try to sit down at the table,

110
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,000
even when I'm on my own.

111
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,850
I like making a pretty plate,

112
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:37,220
taking my time.

113
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:39,000
It makes me happy.

114
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Mathieu: Do you get out the big plates?

115
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:42,630
Léa: Yes.

116
00:04:42,630 --> 00:04:45,510
I deserve a big plate,

117
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:48,090
even for my omelette.

118
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:51,000
Mathieu: I fully support that decision.

119
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,280
Léa: After dinner, I do the washing-up.

120
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:57,000
Well, usually.

121
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Mathieu: That little "usually" hides a story.

122
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Léa: On Sunday, I left a dish to soak all evening.

123
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,120
Mathieu: "Faire tremper" means leaving something in water,

124
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:15,040
to clean it more easily, for example.

125
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:18,350
Léa: Except that in the end, I was looking at the dish as if

126
00:05:18,350 --> 00:05:21,000
it was going to wash itself.

127
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,810
Mathieu: Me too, I'm a big believer

128
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:27,000
in saucepan independence.

129
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Léa: Do you tidy your flat every evening?

130
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,630
Mathieu: No.

131
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:35,000
I mostly tidy what's going to bother me the next day.

132
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,240
A mug on the desk,

133
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:40,000
a bag in the middle of the way.

134
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,090
Léa: I prefer small missions.

135
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,220
I understand.

136
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,870
Once, I decided

137
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:48,000
to tidy a shelf at 9 p.m.

138
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
At 11 p.m., all my books were on the floor.

139
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,280
Mathieu: You'd turned a shelf

140
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,000
into a public library.

141
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,370
Léa: And I no longer knew whether to sort

142
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:03,000
the books by height or by colour.

143
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,150
Mathieu: At that time of night, I suggest sorting them

144
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:10,090
by how close they are to the shelf.

145
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:12,000
Léa: Very practical.

146
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,160
These days, I just put

147
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,000
a few things back in their place.

148
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Then I keep some time for myself.

149
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,690
Mathieu: "Un moment pour moi":

150
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:24,000
it's a very natural expression.

151
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,280
It can be reading, drawing,

152
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,000
listening to an album

153
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
or doing nothing for a few minutes.

154
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Léa: You manage to do nothing?

155
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,090
Mathieu: I'm learning.

156
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,750
At first, I wondered if I was

157
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:41,000
misusing my free time.

158
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,140
Léa: Yes, you can end up wanting

159
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:45,000
to succeed at relaxing too.

160
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Mathieu: Exactly.

161
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,150
So now, some evenings,

162
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:50,400
I sit by the

163
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:54,000
window and listen to what's going on outside.

164
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,280
A bike, people chatting,

165
00:06:57,280 --> 00:07:00,000
someone closing their shutters.

166
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,280
Léa: Me, I like watering my plants and checking whether a

167
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,090
new leaf has grown.

168
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:07,440
Not much happens,

169
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,000
but I like it.

170
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Mathieu: Your plants get a daily report?

171
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,160
Léa: Of course.

172
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:17,000
And they never interrupt me.

173
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Mathieu: Now that's nice.

174
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,750
Léa: To talk about your favourite moment,

175
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:23,650
you can say: "In the evening,

176
00:07:23,650 --> 00:07:26,260
I like taking some time for myself.

177
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:29,090
Usually, I…"

178
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:30,120
Mathieu: My problem

179
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,360
is that my phone takes part

180
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:35,000
in far too many of my "me moments".

181
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Léa: What do you mean?

182
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,890
Mathieu: The other evening, I wanted to check

183
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:42,000
tomorrow's weather.

184
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,700
Twenty minutes later, I was watching

185
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:48,000
someone restore an old chair.

186
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Léa: And the weather?

187
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Mathieu: No idea.

188
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,300
But as for the chair, I think it needed a

189
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:57,090
second coat of paint.

190
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:59,000
Léa: That happens to me too.

191
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I pick up my phone to answer a message,

192
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
then I forget why I picked it up.

193
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Mathieu: Do you do anything to avoid that?

194
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,570
Léa: When I want to read, I leave it on a little table,

195
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:12,000
far from the armchair.

196
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,280
Otherwise, at the slightest difficult passage,

197
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:18,000
I go and check something.

198
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,220
Mathieu: Something very urgent,

199
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:24,090
like the new colour of your cousin's living room.

200
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,160
Léa: Exactly.

201
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:27,000
Sage green, by the way.

202
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Very pretty.

203
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Mathieu: You can say, "I put my phone aside."

204
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:38,450
"Mettre de côté" here means moving something away so

205
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:41,000
you don't deal with it for a while.

206
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:45,240
Léa: During dinner, I put my phone aside.

207
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:49,050
Or I turn off notifications to have some peace.

208
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,950
Mathieu: To have some peace.

209
00:08:50,950 --> 00:08:54,000
I really like that expression.

210
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
You're not necessarily looking for complete silence.

211
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
You just want a bit of calm.

212
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:00,630
Léa: That's it.

213
00:09:00,630 --> 00:09:04,150
And sometimes, I actually use my phone

214
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,000
to listen to music.

215
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,930
I choose what I want to listen to,

216
00:09:08,930 --> 00:09:10,000
then I put it down.

217
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Mathieu: I could try that with an album.

218
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,030
At least there'd be a planned ending.

219
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:19,400
Léa: As long as you don't start looking up the whole

220
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,000
life story of the singer.

221
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Mathieu: You know my weaknesses.

222
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Léa: Let's move on to the bathroom.

223
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Do you shower in the evening or the morning?

224
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Mathieu: In the evening, most of the time.

225
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
I like feeling clean before I put on my pyjamas.

226
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,160
Léa: Me too.

227
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:38,000
And I love the moment when I wash my face.

228
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,950
It's a very simple gesture,

229
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:43,090
but it marks the end of my day out in the world.

230
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:46,000
Mathieu: Do you have lots of products?

231
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,600
Léa: A few.

232
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,000
I take off my make-up if I'm wearing any.

233
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,800
I wash my face,

234
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:52,000
then I put on some cream.

235
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,280
Mathieu: Me, I mostly try not to mix up the

236
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,000
tubes when I'm tired.

237
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Léa: Has that happened to you?

238
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,150
Mathieu: I almost put hand cream

239
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:02,000
on my toothbrush.

240
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Luckily, I read the label.

241
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Léa: A good chance to remind you:

242
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,090
I brush my teeth.

243
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:11,870
In French, we say "les dents",

244
00:10:11,870 --> 00:10:15,000
not "mes dents", in this sentence.

245
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,130
Mathieu: Same for "je me lave le visage"

246
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:19,000
and "je me lave les mains".

247
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,400
Léa: Repeat with us, calmly.

248
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:25,000
I wash my face.

249
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
I brush my teeth.

250
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
I put on my pyjamas.

251
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,160
Mathieu: Careful!

252
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:35,090
Pyjamas don't mean you have to go straight to bed.

253
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:39,000
You can also put them on earlier to be comfortable.

254
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,370
Léa: Mine sometimes starts its shift

255
00:10:41,370 --> 00:10:43,000
right after dinner.

256
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Mathieu: Before going to my bedroom,

257
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,000
I usually get my bag ready,

258
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,840
my keys, my wallet,

259
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:52,000
the documents I need.

260
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Léa: Do you really check everything?

261
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Mathieu: I try.

262
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,020
Once, I left with my lunch

263
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:01,090
and without my computer.

264
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:05,130
Léa: You'd chosen your priorities.

265
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:06,000
Mathieu: A meeting with a box of lentils

266
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
is still tricky.

267
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Léa: Me, I sometimes get my clothes ready,

268
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
especially when I have to leave early.

269
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
In the morning, I don't always feel like

270
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
thinking about an outfit.

271
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Mathieu: "Une tenue" is the set of clothes you're wearing.

272
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:25,100
I'm getting my outfit ready for tomorrow.

273
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,090
Léa: And I look at my diary,

274
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:27,950
but quickly.

275
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:31,000
I want to know what's coming,

276
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
not start working again.

277
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Mathieu: Can you give an example?

278
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,160
Léa: I check the time of an appointment and put the

279
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:40,000
papers I need next to my bag.

280
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Then, it's done.

281
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Mathieu: I like that expression.

282
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
That way, it's done.

283
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,420
You use it when you finish something and

284
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:51,000
no longer need to think about it.

285
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:54,090
Léa: I'm making my lunch tonight.

286
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:56,000
That way, it's done.

287
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Mathieu: To describe the order of your actions,

288
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
you can use four little words.

289
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
First, next, then, finally.

290
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Léa: For example: first, I get my bag ready.

291
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,280
Next, I choose my clothes.

292
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:14,000
Then, I set my alarm.

293
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Finally, I go to my bedroom.

294
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,090
Mathieu: Your turn!

295
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:21,280
Choose two actions from your evening

296
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:25,000
and link them with "d'abord" and "ensuite".

297
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,180
Léa: And once you're in bed,

298
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:29,000
do you fall asleep quickly?

299
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,260
Mathieu: It depends.

300
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:32,000
Sometimes, yes.

301
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Sometimes I suddenly remember

302
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,140
a conversation from Tuesday

303
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:39,000
and finally find the right answer.

304
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,090
Léa: The brilliant answer, three days too late.

305
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,170
Mathieu: Exactly.

306
00:12:44,170 --> 00:12:48,000
My mind has a rather slow delivery service.

307
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Léa: Me, sometimes I think of something I forgot.

308
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,890
So I jot it down in a few words so I can

309
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:57,000
deal with it the next day.

310
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,160
Mathieu: And then?

311
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:00,000
Léa: Sometimes I read.

312
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Sometimes I just stay lying down.

313
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,280
I prefer a book I enjoy coming back to,

314
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:08,090
with fairly short chapters.

315
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:10,830
Mathieu: Me, I've started a detective novel.

316
00:13:10,830 --> 00:13:14,000
Bad idea if I want to stop easily.

317
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,750
Every chapter ends with someone

318
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:19,000
opening a mysterious door.

319
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Léa: And you have to know what's behind it.

320
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:23,740
Mathieu: Always.

321
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:26,000
I'm very polite with mysteries.

322
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
I don't leave them alone in the hallway.

323
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,850
Léa: To talk about tiredness,

324
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:33,150
you can say "j'ai sommeil".

325
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:36,090
It means you feel like sleeping.

326
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:39,000
Mathieu: And "je suis fatigué" is more general.

327
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,890
After a long walk, I can be tired without

328
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:46,000
wanting to sleep right away.

329
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Léa: Another useful difference:

330
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
"Se coucher" and "s'endormir".

331
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,250
Je me couche: I go to bed.

332
00:13:53,250 --> 00:13:57,000
Je m'endors: I start sleeping.

333
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,330
Mathieu: So I can say, "I go to bed around 11

334
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:04,090
but I don't fall asleep straight away."

335
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:06,000
Léa: Exactly.

336
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
And "vers" indicates an approximate time.

337
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,890
"Around 11" isn't necessarily

338
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:15,000
at 11 on the dot.

339
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Mathieu: We've described a fairly calm evening.

340
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:23,150
But yesterday, my neighbour started moving his

341
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:26,000
furniture while I was reading.

342
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,160
Léa: Ah.

343
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:30,020
A quiet little activity.

344
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:34,000
Mathieu: I found out he probably owns 14 chairs.

345
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Léa: Did you go and talk to him?

346
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Mathieu: Yes, nicely.

347
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
I said, "Good evening, sorry, I'm getting up early tomorrow.

348
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,180
Could you make a little less

349
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:47,000
noise?"

350
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Léa: That's a useful sentence.

351
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,660
You explain the situation

352
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,000
and make a polite request.

353
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Mathieu: He apologised.

354
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:59,090
He was looking for a small coin that fell under a piece of furniture.

355
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:03,000
We found it and I could go back to my book.

356
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Léa: My evenings also change when I have friends over.

357
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,540
I'm not going to interrupt

358
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:10,570
a lovely conversation because

359
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:14,000
my diary says "face cream".

360
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,160
Mathieu: Thank goodness.

361
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:20,000
"Thanks for coming, but my face is waiting for me."

362
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,630
Léa: Exactly.

363
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:23,280
A routine can serve as a reference point for us

364
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,090
while staying flexible.

365
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:29,000
Mathieu: And not everyone has the same schedule.

366
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,020
If you work in the evening,

367
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:33,150
if you have young children

368
00:15:33,150 --> 00:15:35,020
or share your home,

369
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:38,000
evenings are different.

370
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,700
Léa: So you can say "en général",

371
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:45,000
"souvent", "parfois" or "ça dépend des jours".

372
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,140
They're very handy words

373
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:49,090
for describing your real life.

374
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:52,260
Mathieu: Now, a little conversation.

375
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:55,000
Léa is going to ask me three questions.

376
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Listen to my answers, then it'll be your turn.

377
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Léa: What do you do after dinner?

378
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,280
Mathieu: Usually, I do the washing-up,

379
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:08,000
then listen to music.

380
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Léa: What helps you relax?

381
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:15,150
Mathieu: I like taking a shower and reading a bit.

382
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:18,090
It helps me think about something else.

383
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:21,000
Léa: And around what time do you go to bed?

384
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,150
Mathieu: I go to bed around 11 on weekdays.

385
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:28,000
At the weekend, it depends.

386
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,120
Léa: Your turn:

387
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:32,000
what do you do after dinner?

388
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Mathieu: What helps you relax?

389
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,720
You can start with "To relax,

390
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,000
I…"

391
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,090
Léa: And around what time do you go to bed?

392
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:48,000
Mathieu: You've just talked about your routine in French.

393
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,540
You can keep your answers and say them again tomorrow

394
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:53,000
with one more little detail.

395
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Léa: For example, add a reason.

396
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,360
I get my clothes ready in the evening because I

397
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:01,000
leave early in the morning.

398
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Mathieu: Or a preference.

399
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:07,090
I prefer reading in bed because I feel good there.

400
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:10,570
Léa: My full version would be: "After dinner,

401
00:17:10,570 --> 00:17:13,000
I tidy the kitchen a bit."

402
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Then, I take some time for myself.

403
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Before going to bed, I brush my teeth

404
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
and get my things ready.

405
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Then I read a few pages.

406
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,410
Mathieu: It's clear, natural, and you can easily

407
00:17:26,410 --> 00:17:29,000
adapt it to your own evening.

408
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:33,090
Léa: Before we go, one last expression.

409
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:34,800
I'm dropping with sleep.

410
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:39,000
It means you really, really want to sleep.

411
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,280
Mathieu: Use it when you're rereading the same sentence

412
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:44,000
for the fourth time.

413
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,400
Léa: Or when you're looking for your glasses

414
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:49,000
while they're on your nose.

415
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Mathieu: That, for me, can happen at any time of day.

416
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,280
Léa: Tell us in the comments which little habit

417
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,090
you love coming back to in the evening.

418
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,500
You can write: "In the evening,

419
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,000
I like … because…"

420
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,980
Mathieu: And if this episode has

421
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:08,950
helped you speak French, you can subscribe to

422
00:18:08,950 --> 00:18:11,000
catch our next conversations.

423
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,270
Léa: Thank you for spending this time with us.

424
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:17,000
Take care and see you very soon!

425
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,840
Mathieu: Have a good evening, good night,

426
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:22,000
depending on when you're listening to us.

427
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:26,090
Léa: And you, Mathieu, are you going to bed now?

428
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:30,000
Mathieu: Yes, I'm taking the direct route.

429
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Léa: Without going via the kitchen?

430
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Mathieu: I'll make an effort.

431
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Good night, Léa!

432
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Léa: Good night, Mathieu!
